[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: weft-agent requirements
VERSION: 0.1 (draft)
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Text

[GRAMMAR]
ELEMENTS:
- TAG: SECTION
  PROPERTIES:
    IS_COMPOSITE: True
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
- TAG: TEXT
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
- TAG: REQUIREMENT
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: STATUS
    TYPE: SingleChoice(Draft, Active, Deleted)
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: VERIFICATION
    TYPE: SingleChoice(Test, Analysis, Inspection, Demonstration)
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: RATIONALE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: SATISFIES
    HUMAN_TITLE: Satisfies (system requirements, weft-design)
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: STANDARDS
    HUMAN_TITLE: Standards (draft mapping)
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: FACTS
    HUMAN_TITLE: Facts (facts.toml in the design repository)
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  RELATIONS:
  - TYPE: Parent
  - TYPE: File

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Component requirements of weft-agent. Each is traced to implementing functions in crates/*/src and to tests in crates/*/tests by relation markers; the gate in crates/weft-agent/tests/requirements.rs fails when an Active requirement verified by Test lacks either. SATISFIES names the system requirements in weft-design/requirements/system.sdoc.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Document sync and decisions

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AGT-001
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Convergence over best-effort transport
STATEMENT: >>>
Nodes shall exchange documents by push and anti-entropy pull (summary, inventory, fetch) so that, once the network allows it, all honest nodes hold the same verified documents, despite loss, delay, reordering, duplicates and partitions.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
SYS-032 permits best-effort transports; correctness must not depend on transport guarantees.
<<<
SATISFIES: SYS-032, SYS-021

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AGT-002
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Content addressing
STATEMENT: >>>
Documents shall be stored by the SHA-256 of their bytes, the digest the verifier uses; a document arriving again over any path shall be dropped.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Several uplinks and relays deliver the same document; deduplication needs no coordination.
<<<
SATISFIES: SYS-005, SYS-032

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AGT-003
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Only verified documents travel
STATEMENT: >>>
A node shall share (advertise, serve, forward) only documents its decider has verified. Intrinsically invalid documents (malformed, bad signature, wrong tenant) shall be quarantined for good; documents of unknown signers or without authorization shall stay local and pending until they verify.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Otherwise any node could inject well-formed documents signed by arbitrary keys and the fleet would store and spread them forever (found by the simulation, 2026-10-20).
<<<
SATISFIES: SYS-021, SYS-016

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AGT-004
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Persist before acting
STATEMENT: >>>
The decider shall save the new verifier state before executing any instruction, and shall execute nothing if saving fails.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Acting on a decision whose anti-rollback state was lost would allow rollback after a crash. The atomic file store itself (docs/11) is still to be built.
<<<
SATISFIES: SYS-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AGT-005
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Path-independent decisions
STATEMENT: >>>
After convergence, every device's installed artifacts, applied configuration, conflicts and withheld components shall equal a fresh evaluation of the same documents, whatever path, order or relay delivered them.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Same inputs, same decision (SYS-017); a malicious relay can only delay (SYS-021).
<<<
SATISFIES: SYS-017, SYS-021

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AGT-006
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Restart recovery
STATEMENT: >>>
A restarted node shall load its saved verifier state, refuse corrupt state, and recover missing documents from peers; until they are back, affected components are withheld.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Restarts must never reset anti-rollback marks or act on incomplete information.
<<<
SATISFIES: SYS-006, SYS-013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AGT-007
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Deterministic simulation
STATEMENT: >>>
The node runtime shall behave deterministically for the same inputs and timing, so that a simulation run can be replayed exactly from its seed.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A failing seed in CI must be reproducible on any developer machine.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AGT-008
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Bounded input from peers
STATEMENT: >>>
Everything a peer sends shall be bounded: document size, number of stored, pending and quarantined documents, and digests per message; malformed messages are dropped.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Peers are untrusted.
<<<
SATISFIES: SYS-016

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AGT-009
STATUS: Active
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Portable topic keys
STATEMENT: >>>
Topic keys shall consist of segments of [a-z0-9_-], within the segment, depth and length limits, so that they are valid on every transport.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Keys must map to MQTT, Zenoh and NATS without escaping.
<<<
SATISFIES: SYS-009
FACTS: pubsub.topic.segment_max, pubsub.topic.max_depth, pubsub.topic.max_len

[[/SECTION]]
